      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the rectangle. We know two things about the backyard:\n\n1. Walking the length 25 times is equivalent to walking a kilometer (1000 meters).\n2. Walking the perimeter 10 times is also equivalent to walking a kilometer (1000 meters).\n\nLet's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) and the width by \\( w \\).\n\nFirst, we use the information about walking the length 25 times:\n\\[ 25l = 1000 \\]\nSolving for \\( l \\):\n\\[ l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\]\nSo, the length of the backyard is 40 meters.\n\nNext, we use the information about walking the perimeter 10 times:\nThe perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[ P = 2l + 2w \\]\nWalking the perimeter 10 times means:\n\\[ 10P = 1000 \\]\nSubstituting \\( P = 2l + 2w \\):\n\\[ 10(2l + 2w) = 1000 \\]\n\\[ 2l + 2w = 100 \\]\nDividing the entire equation by 2:\n\\[ l + w = 50 \\]\nWe already know that \\( l = 40 \\), so we substitute this value into the equation:\n\\[ 40 + w = 50 \\]\nSolving for \\( w \\):\n\\[ w = 50 - 40 = 10 \\]\nSo, the width of the backyard is 10 meters.\n\nNow, we can find the area \\( A \\) of the rectangle using the formula:\n\\[ A = l \\times w \\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( l \\) and \\( w \\):\n\\[ A = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\]\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
