      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the area of Mateen's rectangular backyard, we need to analyze the information given and use it to set up equations. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nAccording to the problem, Mateen can walk the length 25 times or walk the perimeter 10 times to cover 1000 meters. This gives us two pieces of information:\n\n1. The length 25 times is equal to 1000 meters:\n   \\[\n   25l = 1000\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( l \\), we get:\n   \\[\n   l = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\n2. The perimeter walked 10 times is equal to 1000 meters:\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 2(l + w) = 1000\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   10(l + w) = 1000\n   \\]\n   Dividing both sides by 10, we get:\n   \\[\n   l + w = 100\n   \\]\n   Since we already know that \\( l = 40 \\), we can substitute this value into the equation:\n   \\[\n   40 + w = 100\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( w \\), we get:\n   \\[\n   w = 100 - 40 = 60 \\text{ meters}\n   \\]\n\nNow that we have the length and the width of the backyard, we can find the area \\( A \\) using the formula for the area of a rectangle:\n\\[\nA = l \\times w = 40 \\times 60 = 2400 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{2400}\\).",
